                <pb facs="0470" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90G2/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-29T17:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1936—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Your No. 15, June 24, 11 a.m. Department accepts basis of negotiation
                    including reservation with respect to countries formerly included in Ottoman
                    Empire in Asia.</p>
                <p>Draft treaty will be prepared here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
